---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — Peter Kurzok"
  description="Privacy policy for peterkurzok.de — a static site with no cookies, no tracking, and no third-party resources."
>
  <div class="container prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: 2 October 2026</p>

    <p>
      This is a static website. It has no accounts, no login, no contact form, and no
      comment section. Nothing you do here is stored by me beyond what a web server
      unavoidably records in order to send you a page.
    </p>

    <h2>No cookies, no tracking</h2>
    <p>
      This site sets no cookies and uses no analytics, no tracking pixels, and no
      advertising. Every image, style, and script is served from this domain — including
      the small script that opens a photo in the full-screen viewer on the gallery pages —
      and no web fonts are loaded at all. Simply opening a page therefore contacts no
      third-party server. Nothing needs your consent, and there is no consent banner.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting and server logs</h2>
    <p>
      The site is hosted by Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend St., San Francisco, CA 94107,
      USA, acting as a processor on my behalf. To deliver a page and to keep the service
      secure and available, Cloudflare processes technical connection data such as your IP
      address, the requested URL, the time of the request, the referrer, and your browser
      and operating system version.
    </p>
    <p>
      The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR — my legitimate interest in operating a secure,
      functioning website. This data is not merged with other data and is not used to
      identify you. Cloudflare's privacy policy:
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener"
        >cloudflare.com/privacypolicy</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2>Contacting me by email</h2>
    <p>
      If you write to one of the addresses on this site, your message and the data it
      contains are stored so that I can answer it. Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR where
      your request concerns a contract or its initiation, otherwise Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. I
      keep the correspondence for as long as it is needed to deal with your enquiry, and
      longer only where the law requires it.
    </p>

    <h2>External links</h2>
    <p>
      This site links to other websites — Instagram, Flickr, 500px, LinkedIn, GitHub, and
      my app portfolio at apps.peterkurzok.de. Those links are plain links; no content
      from those services is embedded here, so nothing is loaded from them until you
      click. Once you follow a link, the privacy policy of that site applies, not this
      one.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>access the personal data I hold about you (Art. 15)</li>
      <li>have inaccurate data corrected (Art. 16)</li>
      <li>have your data erased (Art. 17)</li>
      <li>have processing restricted (Art. 18)</li>
      <li>receive your data in a portable format (Art. 20)</li>
      <li>object to processing based on legitimate interest (Art. 21)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority, normally
      the data protection authority of the German state in which I am established.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the new version appears on this page with a new date at the
      top.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy:
      <a href="mailto:imprint@peterkurzok.de">imprint@peterkurzok.de</a>. The controller
      and the postal address required by § 5 DDG are given in the
      <a href="/imprint">imprint</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
